# Files that are executed or parsed on the Linux droplet must keep LF endings in
# the WORKING TREE, not just in the blob. This repo is cloned on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites checked-out files to CRLF; the deploy script
# then pushes those working-tree files verbatim to Ubuntu, where a CRLF bash
# script fails as:
#
#     /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# Deliberately narrow. A repo-wide `* text=auto` would renormalize every source
# file on the next checkout, which is a much larger change than this protects
# against.
*.sh                text eol=lf
deploy/Caddyfile*   text eol=lf
deploy/*.service    text eol=lf
deploy/env.*        text eol=lf
